TEST 38099 -- MRP ring switch over with 500ms recovery time
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-30 15:18-15:34 NZDT, tb470, hand-driven (no framework script), queue row 9.
Tester: bench-runner. Case text: AWPTCM-T38099 (ck.db zephyr_cases), 8 steps.

VERDICT: PASS -- labelled CLEAN, graded against the TITLE (500 ms profile, recovery
within 500 ms). 8 switch-overs, copper and fibre, from both ends; one sub-step
UNSUPPORTED; three observations.

  CASE-TEXT DISCREPANCY: the title says 500 ms, but step 7's expected result says
  "Traffic should recover within 200ms" (the same wording as T38098). Per the
  dispatch this is graded against the title. Against the text, 6 of 8 runs meet
  200 ms and 2 do not: the MRC-end copper shuts took 296-304 ms and 406-416 ms.
  Under a 500 ms profile that is expected behaviour, not a fault.

  Every switch-over recovered within 500 ms: worst outage per run 90-416 ms.
  After each shutdown the MRM unblocked its blocked port, showed Open, and traffic
  moved to the other link. No duplicates or echoes during any switch-over.
  UNSUPPORTED (step 8, "Fixed ports"): the IE520-28GSX has no fixed port; the
  SFP/SFP+ copper and fibre legs were measured.

