                     Worst 416 ms (t99g U32), all < 500 ms. PASS
                     Why the MRC-end copper shuts are slow: the MRM's own port1.0.13
                     reports link DOWN late, so the MRM detects the break by missing
                     test frames (50 ms x 5 = 250 ms window plus the switch-over)
                     instead of by the local link event. Stack log for t99g
                     (evidence/38099/t99g/stacklog.out), verbatim:
                       02:32:18 mrpd: EVENT: Rx MRP_LinkDown ring_id=1 port=port4.0.26 ...
                       02:32:18 mrpd: ...: Ring-id[1]: Ring opened
                       02:32:18 mrpd: FSM: ring_id=1 CHK_RC -> CHK_RO evt=MRP_ProtEvTestTimerExpired
                       02:32:18 mrpd: PORT: port1.0.13 link DOWN (0x1003)     <- after the open
                     The MRC's LinkDown frame arrives, but the MRM has React on Link
                     Change: No, so it ignores it. On fibre the MRM's port4.0.26 goes
                     DOWN at once (t99b: "port4.0.26 link DOWN" then "Ring opened").
                     The 200 ms profile's 20 ms x 3 window explains why the same shut
                     took 98-106 ms in 38098.
  8 Fixed + SFP/SFP+ Fixed ports: UNSUPPORTED (no fixed port on the IE520-28GSX). SFP/SFP+
                     copper and fibre: measured in step 7, both PASS (fibre 124-134 ms,
                     copper 90-416 ms). SFP+ at 10G is not measured (the pair links at 1000).

OBSERVATIONS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  O-1  Changing the profile on a live MRM restarts the manager and loops the ring.
       During `profile 500` on the stack (t99cfg, flows running): loop window 79 ms,
       2848 dups, one frame 361x, echoes eth2 2506 / eth3 171, unicast hole up to 196 ms.
       Stack log (evidence/38099/s2-log-u5.out), verbatim:
         02:19:22 mrpd: PORT: Update ring port port1.0.13 with state to Forwarding
         02:19:22 mrpd: PORT: Update ring port port4.0.26 with state to Forwarding
         02:19:22 mrpd: Stopped manager ring-id 1 ...
         02:19:22 mrpd: Started manager ring-id 1 ...
         02:19:22 mrpd: PORT: port 5013 set Forwarding ... port 20026 set Forwarding
         02:19:22 mrpd: FDB: Flush ... / both ring ports Blocked / Ring opened /
                        POWER_ON -> AC_STAT1 -> PRM_UP -> Ring closed -> CHK_RC
       and, interleaved, 8 lines at local7.err:
         EXFX[731]: DBG:_exfx_mcl2_stargv_dbDelete 680: Failed to delete STARGV entry vid 1,
                    grp 0.0.0.0 from exfxStargvList  (+ stargvEntryDelete / mc_entryDelete /
                    mc_route_delete rc=1)
       The same change on the MRC (SA) cost one 8 ms hole and no duplicates.
  O-2  With the 500 ms profile, ring CLOSURE mostly does NOT loop. Only the first restore
       after the profile change looped (t99a: 29 ms, 1000 dups, echoes 517/413,
       TestTimerExpired right after "Ring closed"). The other 7 restores had no
       duplicates, no echoes and no loss. With the 200 ms profile it looped 10 of 10
       (38093-fail.log, 38098.log). So the false test-timer expiry that
       T28863/T38093 report depends on the monitoring window: 60 ms at 200 ms,
       250 ms at 500 ms.
  O-3  The ring ends each restore Closed with the returned port blocked (the MRM keeps
       the path that carried the traffic).

